A||||7||RICK||Gauges
Z||000000||RICK||05-06-99||08:30 AM||||Has anybody put aftermarket gauges in their fiero?  I'm would like to replace the factory gauges with gauges from VDO but I dont know how much trouble I will have using the factory wiring and sensors.  <br>Thanks for any advice.
Z||000001||PaUL||05-06-99||02:27 PM||||Hey I did exactly that, but only my speedo is from VDO the rest are some cheap gauges I got from JCwhittney. The speedo needs to be electrically driven and not the cable driven type. The only problem with doing this is the computer. It gets the vehicle speed from the stock speedo. If you replace it you will need to figure out a way to interface the computer directly to the speed sensor. I think the stock speedo reduces the pulse frequency before sending the signal to the computer. Maybe you could use a decade counting IC.
Z||000002||theogre||05-06-99||08:34 PM||||a flip-flop, and some line drivers, would work. you don't need a counter. The stock speedo only divides by 2.<p>If you are going thru that much trouble, check out Cliff's digital dash. For what you get, it's not that expensive, and it basically drops in.
Z||000003||PaUL||05-07-99||12:49 AM||||Oh yeah Ogre, the old JK flipflop, just use 1 of the outputs. To bad I dropped out of electrical engineering school. 
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||05-07-99||01:50 AM||||The original speedo uses the 4000 ppm from the speed sensor, cleans it up, divides it by two, amplifies it, and sends it back to the ECM. It's not really that hard to build a circuitry to do this but the most effective way is to simply leave the original speedo print untouched. If you strip the print from its gauges, you should still have enough room to add your own speedo. You can then either tap the 4000 ppm or the 2000 ppm signal.<p>Our dashboard also leaves the original speedo print - it's old technology (the original print that is) but it works perfectly. All the other gauges use their own sensors and there's no feedback to the ECM from them.<p>- Cliff<br>PS: Thanks for the plug Ogre! ;)
Z||000005||RICK||05-10-99||08:18 PM||||WHAT????  Could someone please put the above responses into english for me.  I dont know anything about electronics.  What do you mean by "striping".<br>Thanks!
Z||000006||PaUL||05-10-99||09:03 PM||||Behind the dashboard theres a plastic printed circuit. Unlike a printed circuit board, this is a flexible printed circuit.
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||05-11-99||01:34 AM||||Rick, not <b>striping</b> (no idea what that is either), but <b>stripping</b> (surely you know what <b>that</b> is!).
